# image/.dockerignore — what must never bake into the image.
#
# NOTE: Docker only reads `.dockerignore` at the build-context root, so the
# Dockerfile itself uses an explicit COPY list as the real enforcement.
# This file mirrors the repo's two ignore scopes:
# - ../.gitignore — what git won't commit in THIS repo
#   (zsh/local, git/config.local, modules.local.mk, mise.local.toml).
# - ../git/ignore — global excludesFile for every OTHER repo you work in
#   (*.secret, *.env); repeated here so stray local files can't bake in
#   even if someone builds with a dirty worktree.
zsh/local
git/config.local
git/config.env-*
mise.local.toml
modules.local.mk
*.secret
*.env
.whatever/.secret
.git
node_modules
